-- title:
--   Reducedness and Artinianity of a ℚ_q-algebra spanned by an order with nondegenerate trace
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is free and finite as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module, and suppose the trace pairing on $R$ separates points in the sense that for every $r \in R$ with $r \neq 0$ there is $s \in R$ with $\mathrm{Tr}_{R/\mathbb{Z}}(rs) \neq 0$. Let $q$ be a prime, let $T$ be a commutative ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}_q$-algebra structure, and let $f \colon R \to T$ be a ring homomorphism. Assume that the $\mathbb{Q}_q$-subalgebra of $T$ generated by the image of $f$ is all of $T$ (`Algebra.adjoin ℚ_[q] (Set.range f) = ⊤`), and that the family obtained by applying $f$ to the chosen $\mathbb{Z}$-basis of $R$ (`Module.Free.chooseBasis ℤ R`) is linearly independent over $\mathbb{Q}_q$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions about $T$: $T$ is reduced, i.e. its only nilpotent element is $0$, and $T$ is an Artinian ring.
--
--   This is the base-change statement that an order with nondegenerate trace form, mapped into a $\mathbb{Q}_q$-algebra so as to span it and to remain linearly independent, produces a reduced finite-dimensional algebra; in this formalisation it is applied to Hecke algebras acting on the inertia-fixed part of a Tate module, through [`ModularCurve.exists_tateModule_inertia_fixed_linearIndependent_heckeLatticeAlgebra_orbit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_tateModule_inertia_fixed_linearIndependent_heckeLatticeAlgebra_orbit).
